-*   The second `uvec4` of Gaussian $i$ is stored at texture coordinates $(c+1, r)$ [S1, unofficial].
+Each Gaussian $i$ occupies 2 horizontal columns (8 `uint32_t` values, i.e., 2 `uvec4`s).
 
